![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

While removing the strict 72-character limit is beneficial for descriptive titles, completely removing any length constraint from the fallback title generator poses a risk. If a user's first prompt starts with an extremely long single-line input (such as a minified log, a base64 string, or a large JSON payload), the fallback title could become thousands of characters long. This can cause UI rendering issues in OpenCode, database bloat, or issues with terminal title escape sequences. We should enforce a generous but safe maximum limit (e.g., 256 characters) to prevent these edge cases.

```javascript
  const title = titleCaseFirstWord(cleanedTitleLine(firstPromptLine(prompt)));
  const maxLength = 256;
  return title.length <= maxLength ? title : title.slice(0, maxLength - 1).trimEnd() + "…";
```

