![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

To enforce defensive programming and avoid relying on try-catch blocks for handling missing or mock clients (e.g., in testing environments or older host versions), we should explicitly guard against a missing `client` or `client.session.get` method. Checking this upfront at creation time is highly efficient and prevents unnecessary request-time overhead.

```suggestion
export function createSessionStartGreetingGate(client, isHeadless = () => false) {
  const attemptedSessions = new Set();

  if (typeof client?.session?.get !== "function") {
    return async () => false;
  }

  return async function shouldInjectSessionStartGreeting(input) {
```

