The `activeAgentsDir` parameter can be undefined or null in certain execution paths (e.g., if the handler is initialized without it). Passing an undefined value to `join` will throw a `TypeError: Path must be a string`, causing a runtime crash. We should defensively guard against falsy values for `activeAgentsDir` and `runtimeAgentsDir` before calling `join`.

```suggestion
export function readAidevopsVersion(activeAgentsDir, runtimeAgentsDir = activeAgentsDir) {
  const activeVersion = activeAgentsDir ? readIfExists(join(activeAgentsDir, "VERSION")) : "";
  if (activeVersion) return activeVersion;
  if (process.env.AIDEVOPS_VERSION?.trim()) return process.env.AIDEVOPS_VERSION.trim();

  const candidates = runtimeAgentsDir ? [
    join(runtimeAgentsDir, "VERSION"),
    join(runtimeAgentsDir, "..", "VERSION"),
    join(runtimeAgentsDir, "..", "version"),
  ] : [];
```

