@gemini-code-assist This is an additive micro-optimization rather than a correctness defect. The current function only scans the bounded paths extracted from one issue (`.agents/scripts/verify-issue-close-helper.sh:267-286`), and the proposed `local -A` implementation is incompatible with the repository Bash 3.2 requirement (`.agents/reference/bash-compat.md:73`). Keeping the portable implementation and PR scope unchanged; a follow-up optimization is only warranted if profiling identifies this bounded loop as material.

Verified: `bash .agents/scripts/tests/test-verify-issue-close-helper-pr-files.sh` (4/4 pass), `shellcheck` on both changed shell files (clean), and `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` (clean).

