![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Synchronous filesystem operations like `closeSync` can throw errors (e.g., if the file descriptor is invalid or already closed). Since this is inside a `finally` block, any unhandled exception thrown here will propagate and could crash the application.

It is safer to wrap `closeSync` in a `try-catch` block to ensure that any errors during cleanup are gracefully ignored, in line with the best-effort nature of terminal title synchronization.

```javascript
  } finally {
    if (ttyFd !== undefined) {
      try {
        closeSync(ttyFd);
      } catch {
        // ignore
      }
    }
  }
```

