![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

In `setStatus(nextStatus)`, the check `if (!nextLabel || nextLabel === terminalTitleStatusLabel(status))` prevents updating the status to any value that maps to an empty label (such as an untracked, completed, or paused status). Once a status prefix (like `[RUN]` or `[WAIT]`) is set, it can never be cleared or removed back to a plain title without calling `reset()` (which also clears the base title).

We can simplify and improve this by comparing the resolved labels directly, allowing the status prefix to be cleared when transitioning to a status with an empty label.

```javascript
    setStatus(nextStatus) {
      const nextLabel = terminalTitleStatusLabel(nextStatus);
      const currentLabel = terminalTitleStatusLabel(status);
      if (nextLabel === currentLabel) return false;
      status = nextStatus;
      return render();
    },
```
